## The C runtime tables of variadic functions (ImplementationPlan.md 5.15.2
## 'Lowering in the backend' tables and 'Link time (msil-ld)' rules 2, 3, 5
## and 6; M26.c, M26.d; recon p3 variadics 2.4). A program calls every
## function of a C runtime's va_list variant table and of its fixed-arity
## list, through a variadic declaration, and links against a native stand-in
## that defines each function and each variant. --print-imports lists every
## call, sorted by symbol: a variadic function binds the P/Invoke of its C
## name to its va_list variant ('printf -> libc.so.6!vprintf'), a
## fixed-arity one binds to itself. The linked text's P/Invokes take the
## va_list (native int) for the variadic functions, as 'as "<variant>"', and
## the call's fixed arguments for the fixed-arity ones. Runtimes
## (getCRuntime):
## - Glibc, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu-msil: the 44 variant pairs and the 25
##   fixed-arity names;
## - Musl, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl-msil: the Glibc pairs without the
##   __isoc* and _chk names (21);
## - Msvcrt, x86_64-pc-windows-gnu-msil: the 64 variant pairs and the 62
##   fixed-arity names;
## - UCRT, x86_64-pc-windows-msvc-msil: no variants (its printf family is
##   inline C) and the 30 fixed-arity names: its 20 variadic exports and the
##   POSIX names of 10 of them (execl, execle, execlp, execlpe, open, sopen,
##   spawnl, spawnle, spawnlp, spawnlpe), which the UCRT headers declare as
##   variadic and oldnames.lib maps to the underscore exports (plan section
##   12, '5.15.2's fixed-arity list amended (UCRT)'); the stand-in ucrt.def
##   exports all 30.
## clone and makecontext, on no list, are native-variadic.test's.
## gen.py holds the lists (sorted, no name on both, as the backend asserts)
## and writes each runtime's program, native stand-in and expectations.
## Both link paths: CIL objects from llc, and bitcode through
## --lto-emit-asm. The backend (MSILVariadics.cpp) and msil-ld
## (lld/MSIL/Variadics.cpp) each keep a copy of the lists: an object call is
## FIXED_ARITY only by the backend's copy, and the linked text's by
## msil-ld's, so the two paths check every listed name in both copies.

